{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r2","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:49:14.252Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"307628bd63ee9282a2f931ab77fcbbdc1edd2af76b78bcb03eaef202fe73113a","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, here's the list for Kwame's account review. It comes from #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet. I left out everything on Pellow Home Living.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- **Ticket #4419** (Moss's Coastal cheat sheet): the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. It is listed as still open.\n- **Ticket PD-8841** (your 2025-12-08 cutover recap): Pemberline Dock handles chassis pool holds badly on double-booked gates, specifically Gate 4B. That recap is a public note, not one of Moss's.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- **Feature request #882** (Moss's cheat sheet): warehouse managers want a bulk-clear button for departed barges.\n- **Ticket #4419** (Moss's 2025-11-02 digest): this one is barge slip 7 schedule sync, and DMF also asked for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift. The digest puts it under the Puget Sound account, which the cheat sheet identifies as DMF.\n- **No ticket number:** the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch.\n\n**Check before the review:** #4419 appears under both accounts. The cheat sheet puts it on PHL (report timeout) and the Nov 2 digest puts it on DMF (slip 7 sync). I can't tell which is right, or whether it's a typo or two different tickets, so I've listed it under both. Kwame should confirm.\n\n**Left out:** PD-4821 and #8812 are Pellow Home Living, PD-4824 and PD-4827 are Saltmarsh Provisions, and those are the only ticket numbers I saw outside the two accounts. #coastal-team and #coastal-random have nothing on PHL or DMF. The account ticket folders aren't visible to me, so this list covers only what was mentioned in the channels and notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
